### What does guaranteed delivery mean?

Guaranteed delivery means a produced record is reliably persisted and eventually processed, with no silent loss and no unhandled failure. No single setting provides it; it is a coordinated stack across the whole path.

```java
package com.bank.delivery;

public class GuaranteedDeliveryStack {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Guaranteed delivery = three layers:");
        System.out.println("  1. PRODUCER: acks=all + min.isr + idempotence + retries");
        System.out.println("  2. CONSUMER: manual commit + read_committed + idempotent processing");
        System.out.println("  3. OPERATIONAL: dead letter queue + monitoring");
        System.out.println();
        System.out.println("Any weak link breaks the guarantee.");
    }
}
```

```text
Guaranteed delivery = three layers:
  1. PRODUCER: acks=all + min.isr + idempotence + retries
  2. CONSUMER: manual commit + read_committed + idempotent processing
  3. OPERATIONAL: dead letter queue + monitoring

Any weak link breaks the guarantee.
```

### How do you configure the producer?

```java
package com.bank.producer;

import org.apache.kafka.clients.producer.ProducerConfig;
import java.util.Properties;

public class GuaranteedProducerConfig {
    public static Properties config() {
        Properties props = new Properties();
        props.put(ProducerConfig.BOOTSTRAP_SERVERS_CONFIG,
            "broker1:9092,broker2:9092");
        props.put(ProducerConfig.KEY_SERIALIZER_CLASS_CONFIG,
            "org.apache.kafka.common.serialization.StringSerializer");
        props.put(ProducerConfig.VALUE_SERIALIZER_CLASS_CONFIG,
            "org.apache.kafka.common.serialization.StringSerializer");

        // Durability
        props.put(ProducerConfig.ACKS_CONFIG, "all");

        // Idempotence (prevents retry duplicates)
        props.put(ProducerConfig.ENABLE_IDEMPOTENCE_CONFIG, "true");

        // Retries bounded by delivery timeout
        props.put(ProducerConfig.RETRIES_CONFIG, Integer.MAX_VALUE);
        props.put(ProducerConfig.DELIVERY_TIMEOUT_MS_CONFIG, 120000);

        // Max in-flight for idempotence
        props.put(ProducerConfig.MAX_IN_FLIGHT_REQUESTS_PER_CONNECTION, 5);

        return props;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Properties p = config();
        System.out.println("Producer config for guaranteed delivery:");
        System.out.println("  acks             = " + p.get(ProducerConfig.ACKS_CONFIG));
        System.out.println("  idempotence      = " + p.get(ProducerConfig.ENABLE_IDEMPOTENCE_CONFIG));
        System.out.println("  retries          = MAX");
        System.out.println("  delivery.timeout = 120s");
    }
}
```

```text
Producer config for guaranteed delivery:
  acks             = all
  idempotence      = true
  retries          = MAX
  delivery.timeout = 120s
```

### How do you configure the consumer?

```java
package com.bank.consumer;

import org.apache.kafka.clients.consumer.ConsumerConfig;
import java.util.Properties;

public class GuaranteedConsumerConfig {
    public static Properties config() {
        Properties props = new Properties();
        props.put(ConsumerConfig.BOOTSTRAP_SERVERS_CONFIG, "broker1:9092");
        props.put(ConsumerConfig.GROUP_ID_CONFIG, "settlement-service");
        props.put(ConsumerConfig.KEY_DESERIALIZER_CLASS_CONFIG,
            "org.apache.kafka.common.serialization.StringDeserializer");
        props.put(ConsumerConfig.VALUE_DESERIALIZER_CLASS_CONFIG,
            "org.apache.kafka.common.serialization.StringDeserializer");

        // Manual commit -- only after processing succeeds
        props.put(ConsumerConfig.ENABLE_AUTO_COMMIT_CONFIG, "false");

        // Read only committed transaction records
        props.put(ConsumerConfig.ISOLATION_LEVEL_CONFIG, "read_committed");

        // Start from earliest if no committed offset
        props.put(ConsumerConfig.AUTO_OFFSET_RESET_CONFIG, "earliest");

        return props;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Consumer config for guaranteed delivery:");
        System.out.println("  auto.commit   = false");
        System.out.println("  isolation     = read_committed");
        System.out.println("  offset.reset  = earliest");
    }
}
```

```text
Consumer config for guaranteed delivery:
  auto.commit   = false
  isolation     = read_committed
  offset.reset  = earliest
```

### How do you configure the topic?

```bash
# Create topic with replication and min ISR
kafka-topics --create --topic transfers \
  --partitions 6 --replication-factor 3

kafka-configs --alter --topic transfers \
  --add-config min.insync.replicas=2
```

```java
package com.bank.topic;

public class TopicConfig {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Topic config for guaranteed delivery:");
        System.out.println("  partitions          = 6");
        System.out.println("  replication.factor  = 3");
        System.out.println("  min.insync.replicas = 2");
    }
}
```

